{
  "id": "squarp.hapax",
  "maker": "Squarp Instruments",
  "model": "Hapax",
  "category": "sequencer",
  "summary": "A two-project hardware sequencer with eight tracks per project, driving MIDI and CV/gate at once. Its output is time: notes, gates and clock. All connections are on the rear. The panel is drawn as a desktop sequencer: two displays over a step matrix, with the encoders between them. The matrix is drawn at the arrangement rather than counted off the product, so treat the grid as a caricature; the sockets and their sides are the part this entry is detailed about. The eight encoders under the displays move, and the track pads send MIDI.",
